Privacy Policy for Super Pixel Knight: Retro Adventure
Effective Date: October 3, 2026
This Privacy Policy governs your use of the mobile application Super Pixel Knight: Retro Adventure ("App") with package name com.superpixelknight.retroadventure, developed by Super Pixel Knight Studio ("we", "our", or "us").
We are committed to protecting your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains what information is collected, how it is used, and your choices regarding your data.
1. Information Collection and Storage
Local Storage (Game Progress & Preferences)
Super Pixel Knight: Retro Adventure stores your game progress, best scores, unlocked levels, last played level, and audio/sound settings locally on your device using Android's SharedPreferences.
•
This data remains strictly on your device.
•
We do not transmit, collect, or store your gameplay data or personal scores on any external servers.
•
If you uninstall the app, this local data is deleted.
2. Third-Party Services (Advertising & Consent)
To keep Super Pixel Knight: Retro Adventure free to play, we integrate third-party advertising SDKs that may collect certain information to serve ads.
Google AdMob & User Messaging Platform (UMP)
•
AdMob: We use Google AdMob to display banner advertisements, interstitial ads between levels, and rewarded video ads. Google AdMob may use device identifiers, IP addresses, and ad interaction data to serve relevant ads.
•
Consent (GDPR / CCPA): For users in the European Economic Area (EEA), UK, and other regions subject to privacy regulations, we use the Google User Messaging Platform (UMP) SDK to present a consent management prompt. You can review, grant, or withdraw your consent at any time by accessing the Settings menu in the game.
For more information on how Google uses data when you use our app, please visit Google's Privacy & Terms.
3. Children's Privacy
Super Pixel Knight: Retro Adventure is a family-friendly game suitable for all ages. We do not knowingly collect personally identifiable information from children under the age of 13. If you are a parent or guardian and believe your child has provided personal information to a third-party ad network, please review Google AdMob's child-directed settings and privacy guidelines.
4. Security
We take reasonable measures to protect the security of your information. Because gameplay data is stored locally and advertising is handled securely through Google's industry-standard AdMob SDK, your interaction with the app is secure.
5. Changes to This Privacy Policy
We may update our Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted on this page with an updated effective date. You are advised to review this Privacy Policy periodically for any changes.
